      ],
      "id" : "5EEB4EB7-3F2C-4983-A8DF-DA2FB92C12CC",
      "note" : "# Noisy Dot Sphere\n\nEach vertex of an icosphere is a dot. **Noise Field** (Gradient Noise\n3D) samples smooth fractal noise at every dot. **Displace** pushes each\ndot out or in along its radius by that value and swells the dots on\nthe crests.\n\nThe noise is sampled in 3D, so it has no UV seam or pole pinch. Its\n**Drift** times **Time** moves the field through the sphere.\n\nOn Noise Field, **Frequency** sets how many lumps there are and\n**Octaves** how much fine detail. On Displace, **amount** is the\ndisplacement as a fraction of the radius, **radius** the dot size and\n**swell** how much bigger the dots get on the crests. Keep\n**radius x (1 + swell x 0.5)** below about half the dot spacing (0.035)\nor neighbouring dots touch."
    }
  ],
  "requiredPlugins" : [
    {
      "id" : "graphics.fabric.CoreNodes"
    }
